gm&amp;quot;, but it's a concept that has gotten lost for lack of a name in M20.... The Hermetics are definitely spot on about some things), is pretty much total crap for others. It's a REALLY bad fit to force some types of characters to depend on Harvey for their even having the ability to alter reality. It doesn't fit into the way they Awakening, their Focus, their Seekings, etc. It's 100% forcing an ill-fitting game concept onto a character and straight-jacketing pretty much every thing about their character that is magical. <br /> <br /> That's why the Guide to the Technocracy spent a lot of time showing several different ways that the Union minimizes and marginalizes their Geniuses. That's why the types of Avatar you are talking about used to require a Merit. They weren't the default. That's why there was another Merit to buy the chance to have the Avatar not be this other thing you ever had to really deal with. That's why the description of the ways Avatars manifested based on Essence wasn't always, or even often, about a person, particularly one that the mage dealt with regularly. It could just as easily be a noise or a book or a vague feeling or the way events happened around the character, etc. <br /> <br /> Avatars are what you make of them. And you can make absolutely nothing of them at all and have a Mage game that may be &amp;quot;ideologically impure&amp;quot; but it can be just as strong, perhaps even stronger and better for some chronicle ideas, than having them. You can also go completely the other way and have Avatars be even more intrinsic and involved than your method (How about setting up a collaberative &amp;quot;Avatar-Guiding&amp;quot; system based around something like Shadow-Guiding from Wraith? Why not?) However, those are very particular games with a very particular feel. <br /> <br /> The NWO is my current game is MUCH better off not having to deal with/not deal with a Genius, particularly of your invisible, bossy and maybe-potentially-helpful-if they-feel-like-it friend variety. The perhaps-a-Son-of-Ether and the Hermetic could probably have them and still function as is, but it would be something grafted on that doesn't need to be there for the characters to function and would probably get in the way of the way the characters have been played to date. The Cultist and the Verbena could integrate such an Avatar best, particularly the Cultist, but they have other things going on, so, though it might add, it would take time away from some of their other concerns. The pyromaniac Akashic former Kopa Loei has a Totem that does what you're talking about, only not very often... And it works out great for that character. THAT character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> I just think it's a shame when an aspect of gameplay is removed because one personaly feels that they can't use it efectively, and then tries to advocate against using it at all.<br /> <br /> If it's just for this specific group and this particular player, then fine. Do as is needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T13:07:33-08:00","id":1014907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1013862-help-how-to-roleplay-seekings?p=1014868#post1014868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough.<br /> <br /> I just think it's a shame when an aspect of gameplay is removed because one personaly feels that they can't use it efectively, and then tries to advocate against using it at all.<br /> <br /> If it's just for this specific group and this particular player, then fine. Do as is needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not necessarily removed, per se. As Tuch pointed out, Avatars don't get play a lot of the time. They don't even get mentioned in a lot of the examples of play for Mage games or most of the Mage fiction (for what it's worth... though there some excellent examples of Avatars in a few stories). I know about Amanda's/Mercy's Avatar. but I can't recall what John Courage's is. Or Dante's? We saw some things about both of Heylal Theomin's, before the Gilgul? But what about Porthos's (and we have a chunk of a book about him). Similarly, what about Voormas? <br /> <br /> As far as consistency in having Avatars described and integrated, the only time I've seen it followed through an entire group is probably with the M20 Quickstart, but I'm not going to pull out the Book of Chantries to check. <br /> <br /> Avatars all too often end up like D&amp;D animal companions and familiars. They disappear until someone remembers they exist. Most of the time, I've seen them used (and used them myself) as something that only appears at Seekings. Or, VERY RARELY, at other times. And then everyone knows that something important is happening... A few times they have been integrated into play as important factors, most notably in a game or so in which started with the characters' Awakenings. <br /> <br /> So it's not removing an aspect of gameplay. It's whether you want to emphasize it or not. Not everything in the game is emphasized by every group (or even the same group in different chronicles). In fact, not everything in Mage CAN be used in a Mage game. Particularly the bits that completely are completely at odds. I'm sure there are a several to a crap ton of rules in M20 you're ignoring in your game as well or not using to their extent of their fullest write-up or potention. Just not this particular one and not this particular aspect of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T14:14:42-08:00","id":1014954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1013862-help-how-to-roleplay-seekings?p=1014907#post1014907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not necessarily removed, per se. As Tuch pointed out, Avatars don't get play a lot of the time. They don't even get mentioned in a lot of the examples of play for Mage games or most of the Mage fiction (for what it's worth... though there some excellent examples of Avatars in a few stories). I know about Amanda's/Mercy's Avatar. but I can't recall what John Courage's is. Or Dante's? We saw some things about both of Heylal Theomin's, before the Gilgul? But what about Porthos's (and we have a chunk of a book about him). Similarly, what about Voormas?<br /> <br /> As far as consistency in having Avatars described and integrated, the only time I've seen it followed through an entire group is probably with the M20 Quickstart, but I'm not going to pull out the Book of Chantries to check.<br /> <br /> Avatars all too often end up like D&amp;D animal companions and familiars. They disappear until someone remembers they exist. Most of the time, I've seen them used (and used them myself) as something that only appears at Seekings. Or, VERY RARELY, at other times. And then everyone knows that something important is happening... A few times they have been integrated into play as important factors, most notably in a game or so in which started with the characters' Awakenings.<br /> <br /> So it's not removing an aspect of gameplay. It's whether you want to emphasize it or not. Not everything in the game is emphasized by every group (or even the same group in different chronicles). In fact, not everything in Mage CAN be used in a Mage game. Particularly the bits that completely are completely at odds. I'm sure there are a several to a crap ton of rules in M20 you're ignoring in your game as well or not using to their extent of their fullest write-up or potention. Just not this particular one and not this particular aspect of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably that's part of the nature of the Avatar. Some mages have it so strong that they literally can't go a day without them coming in and rearanging their life, others wonder if they have an avatar at all.<br /> <br /> The game I'm currently running has avatars used quite extensively for various things.<br /> <br /> One has a Primordial avatar which is the spirit of Excalibur, who berates their mage often for choosing to avoid conflict and battle. The player then has to question, do they try to apease their avatar, or do they stay true to themselves? Is there a away to do both?<br /> <br /> One has a Dynamic avatar which comes up in the form of music, shapes in their cigarette smoke. But sometimes it's just intuitions and feelings, for example the sudden instinct to look out the window just in time to see a group of technocrats approach the building, or a burning desire to return to the scene of the crime just to give it a second look. Problem is that because of the dynamic nature of their avatar, the question on whether or not all these intuitions add up to anything or not is always present.<br /> <br /> One has a Questing avatar which if pushing them to pursue what happened to their parents, regardless of whether it helps them on their current goal or not. The player then has to choose whether to follow this push and satisfy their personal curiosity, or ignore their avatar and stay on course with what they are trying to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> I use them to add an extra personal level to each player, and provide for them a conflict which may get in the way of the events of the story, or even lead them completely down the wrong path. The avatar may wear the clothes of a spiritual guide, but it is just as self serving as it is insightful.<br /> <br /> Another thing that the Avatar allows is for Pathos towards Widderslainte. In fact, the entire tragedy of a widderslainte falls apart without recognising the avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T16:43:09-08:00","id":1015005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1013862-help-how-to-roleplay-seekings?p=1014954#post1014954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Another thing that the Avatar allows is for Pathos towards Widderslainte. In fact, the entire tragedy of a widderslainte falls apart without recognising the avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah... The tragedy of Widderslainte (if that's the way you want to play them astragic... since they can just be creepy evil psycho murder-tots) is that they were corrupt before they were born and might, probably, unless that's what the game is about, be irredeemable. None of which requires Avatars. <br /> <br /> They can just as easily require reincarnation/transmigration of a tainted soul. (Maybe not even that...) (Probably, as a prerequisite, the existence of something like a &quot;soul&quot;). Avatars might or might not be souls. In fact, a lot of views on the Avatar specifically say they aren't souls. They might be weird extradimensional parasites that use humans in a Dawkins-esque &quot;Selfish Gene&quot; way to enact their plans. They may be pieces of dead angels. Those two may be the same thing. Or bits of God. Or self-delusion because the ability to manipulate reality causes a psychotic break and mages are all schizophrenic. <br /> <br /> They may be any number of things, but you don't need to have Avatars to have Widderslainte.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T11:11:01-08:00","id":1015742,"title":"","content":"<i>I made a mistake posting this on another thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay. Thank you for your answers. My game was yesterday and I decided to go for a narrative description of the Seekings of my players. I will tell you some of what I said :</i><br /> <br /> <i>- The Virtual Adept (a hacker): He received an e-mail without object nor sender, and with an only link towards a website with a 1 hour countdown that begun the moment he was on the site. A door oped on the screen and he clicked on it. Then he entered a complex code that he was to hack, a code with multiple security protocols sent by his Avatar. This was a metaphor of his mind and each block that he passed opened a world of possibilities, making him closer to the next level of Enlightment. In the end, he made the necessary effort and managed to pass many blocks and the Avatar granted him that next level.</i><br /> <br /> <i>- The Cultist (a singer): She was preparing for a concert when the world begun to blur around her and suddenly she was on a stage in front of what she understood was the sad and giving up humanity. Fueled by the desire to help men and women let go of the fear and to give them the hope to go forward, she begun to sing, shortly followed by a man looking much like Freddy Mercury (her Avatar). Step by step, she was to guide humanity towards the state of awareness of their own abilities to help them understand that they matter and that they can do something about their lives. It was a song of hope and magick.</i><br /> <br /> <i>- The Hermetic (an alchemist): In a dream, he traveled the maze of his own mind, guided by a man that looked much like him, only much older (his Avatar) through his memories. In each memory he grasped a little more of the signification of each event, unraveling the misteries of each place he went, each person he met, seeing powerful mystic threads, symbols and characters of ancient langages. He awakened with a new knowledge of how the world functions and how to make it his.</i><br /> <br /> <i>- The Hollow One (a poet): His Avatar is a muse having the shape of a beatiful woman with tatoos of inspiring words and phrases that she only let him see from far, feeding his passion, his inpiration and fueling his own madness. But in this dream, she let him go closer, authorizing him to touch her. They had a carnal and sensual relation that particular night where she let him scouring her body and learn new concepts to inspire his Work on a deeper level. But she would not let him know of all her intimity, only showing certain parts of her body, thus only parts of the words and phrases she had on her. He awakened with a new look on the world.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Thank you again !</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T13:12:36-08:00","id":1015800,"title":"","content":"Those sound really good. Its hard sometimes to know how far to go or not go in the narative which largely depends on the level of Arete they will be obtaining. By Arete 5 most of the gloves have come off as they begin to realize that Magick is more about force of will upon reality than the tools needed to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T13:47:53-08:00","id":1015818,"title":"","content":"If you and the players enjoyed it, then all went well.<br /> <br /> My after-the-fact advice is to write down what happened in as much detail as you can. It's a great place to start from for the next set of Seekings. <br /> <br /> For the Hermetic, the next Seeking may be to see that the maze he wandered was only one level of a larger complex... or that he mispercieved the maze as a static thing and that it changes... to advance he must now figure out how and why... or that three dimensions was too limiting and next time it's going to be a Dr. Strange-esque series of non-linear connecting scenes of completely different types of realities... or its like Door's Progressive House from Neverwhere<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> Each Revelation building on the last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T14:41:46-08:00","id":1015856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1013862-help-how-to-roleplay-seekings?p=1015818#post1015818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Hermetic, the next Seeking may be to see that the maze he wandered was only one level of a larger complex... or that he mispercieved the maze as a static thing and that it changes... to advance he must now figure out how and why... or that three dimensions was too limiting and next time it's going to be a Dr. Strange-esque series of non-linear connecting scenes of completely different types of realities... or its like Door's Progressive House from Neverwhere<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> Each Revelation building on the last.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that idea thanks ^^<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T09:33:46-08:00","id":1016140,"title":"","content":"Put a few ideas down for each NOW while you are still in the afterglow of the Seeking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}